"about": "Modern-era player finalists for each Pro Football Hall of Fame class, from a news report of that year's finalists (facts only: who was a finalist that year). Kept by hand (Oct 31, 2026, the owner 5:13 pm: \"snubs\"); profootballhof.com's terms (effective Feb 24, 2026, §3) forbid gathering its content, and NFL.com recaps are off limits, so none are used. Coaches, contributors and senior finalists are left out. The nflhof job drops anyone the Wikipedia inductee category lists as elected, so a finalist who is later elected falls off by himself. A name is a Wikipedia page title (add the title in brackets when the plain name is ambiguous). Classes 2002-2026 so far (2005 and 2006 reports name only part of the list — marked \"partial\"); 2008 added Nov 5 (the 17-finalist list; seniors Marshall Goldberg and Emmitt Thomas and commissioner Paul Tagliabue left out); 1999-2001 added Nov 5 (2000 partial: the report names only the finalists it mentions; seniors Nick Buoniconti 2001, Dave Wilcox 2000, Billy Shaw 1999, coaches and owners left out); no report found yet for 1998 or earlier (players' own Wikipedia pages still count for those years). Senior finalists are left out where the report marks them; the job also drops any year more than 30 seasons after a player's last season. Add a class each winter when the finalists are announced.",
